WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.339
Severe economic sanctions on Putin

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.739
and all those folks around him

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.869
choking off access to technology

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.699
as well as cutting off access to

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.709
the global financial system

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.839
has had a profound impact already.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.279
In response to the brutal,

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.199
unprovoked and illegal invasion of

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.479
Ukraine, the U.S., the UK

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.099
and countries in the European Union

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.049
have effectively cut Russia out

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.939
of the global financial system.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.619
Germany suspended construction of

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.269
the Nord Stream 2 natural gas

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.739
pipeline and is talking about

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.239
beefing up its military.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.069
Italy and France are seizing yachts

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.229
and other assets of Russian citizens

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.069
on the grounds that their

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.989
kleptocrats profiting from an

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.039
outlaw regime.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.869
The US Congress is contemplating a

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.429
bill that would let the government

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.409
grab Russian assets in America

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.359
above $5 million and use

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.309
the proceeds to aid Ukraine.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:48.809
A slew of private companies have

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.609
also voluntarily withdrawn from

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.349
Russia. Apple and Google Pay have

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.389
stopped working on the Moscow Metro.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:56.249
Russian filmmakers with ties to

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.839
the government have been disinvited

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.579
from showing their work abroad.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.679
The International Cat Federation

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.509
has banned Russian felines

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:04.619
from competition.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.599
Such actions are, of course,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.189
understandable in the face of

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:10.169
unjustifiable aggression.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.119
But will they actually work to

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.039
facilitate Russia's withdrawal

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.019
from Ukraine or weaken

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.479
Vladimir Putin's regime?

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.459
If history is any guide, the simple

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.869
answer is no.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.149
And not only that, they will mostly

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.829
harm the already long suffering

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.989
people of Russia and quite possibly

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.119
be used to justify even more

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.189
egregious behavior on the part

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:32.969
of Putin.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.369
Historically, sanctions, especially

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.379
in authoritarian regimes, often

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.359
galvanize the targeted countries.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.399
For instance, US economic sanctions

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:43.199
on imperial Japan before World War

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.329
Two were taken as an act of war

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.889
and encouraged more repression at

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.839
home and expansion abroad.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.029
In October 2019, Government

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.769
Accountability Office report found

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.899
that sanctions often have unintended

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.939
consequences, including negative

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.009
impacts on human rights or public

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.839
health. Sanctions against Cuba,

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.699
Iran and Venezuela haven't had

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.859
the desired effects of regime change

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.239
and liberalization.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.859
In fact, they've served as a

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.929
scapegoat for bad economic

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.609
and police state policies.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.469
Sanctions don't work because there's

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.419
almost always workarounds, notes

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.219
Johns Hopkins economist Steve

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:18.989
Hankey. That's especially true in

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.969
the current case, with China and

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.859
India largely abstaining from the

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.239
Western response.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.219
And why punish regular citizens

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.589
in autocratic regimes for the crimes

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.239
of their unelected leaders?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.189
Everyday Russians, thousands of

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.359
whom have been imprisoned for

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.759
protesting, are also victims

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.989
of Putin's madness.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.759
Private companies opting to withdraw

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.589
from Russia voluntarily is

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.299
less objectionable than government

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.799
mandated sanctions.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.659
But it's also not clear what

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.609
they accomplish other than stoking

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.649
jingoism and punishing innocent

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:51.629
people. Backing Putin into

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.489
a corner politically isn't going

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.839
to lead him to retreat.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.249
Rather than doubling down on

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.259
sanctions and promising ever more

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.059
draconian measures, the Biden

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.709
administration should be developing

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:04.139
off ramps or ways to de-escalate

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.239
the conflict by giving Putin some

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:07.769
sort of face saving measure to

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.899
withdraw or abide by a settlement

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.549
that gives maximum peace and safety

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.769
to Ukraine and stability to Europe

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.239
and the rest of the world.

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.339
In all likelihood, there is no

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.899
perfect solution.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.909
But as our experience of the past 20

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.069
years should remind us, foreign

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.199
policy is ultimately not a game

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.299
of good triumphing over evil

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.219
or idealism winning out over

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.329
realism.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.159
It's about making the world a better

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.229
place, not a perfect

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.230
place.

